  "description": "The 2026 Rhode Island gubernatorial election will be held on November 3, 2026, to elect the governor of Rhode Island. Incumbent Democratic Governor Dan McKee is seeking a second full term and faces a competitive primary challenge from former CVS Health executive Helena Foulkes, who led him by 20 points in a May 2026 Emerson College/WPRI poll. On the Republican side, a multi-candidate primary includes Elaine Pelino, Aaron Guckian, and Robert Raimondo, while independent candidate Ken Block is also running. The race will determine leadership for a state that has leaned Democratic in recent presidential elections but has a history of electing independent-minded governors.",
